WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:07.520
As we cast our eyes above to the boundless sky, we know

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:15.570
Whatever tomorrow brings, the sun will always shine

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.660
So won't you come with me?

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.720
It's almost time for the school bell to ring

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.930
And every moment by moment

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.350
I feel more and more like I could fly

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.810
This feeling fills my thoughts and sets my heart alight

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.270
It's this moment I love most of all

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:52.940
In my bag I hold all the things I've overcome

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:56.700
And on their wings, I'll fly into the future

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.200
We can do anything, at any time and any place

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.710
And no one can stop us even if they try

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:09.340
From ING and that alone can we proceed

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:13.260
Carrying all our feelings as we go

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.260
Flying with our dreams for all to see

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:23.730
Let's close today's chapter, and start a new page!

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.990
Lookin' good.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:41.490
Really good, Sixteen-chan.

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:44.040
Okay, strike a pose for me.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:45.660
Nice.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.790
That's great.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.040
Brush your hair back.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.790
Perfect. Now look over here.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.130
Sixteen-chan's on the cover again.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.340
Wasn't she just the cover girl recently?

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:00.970
So cool...

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.890
You're into this?

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:03.810
Yeah.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:07.350
The M16 family's pretty popular.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.190
Oh hey, Eighteen.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:10.400
Good morning—

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.730
Wait, aren't you a part of that family?

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:14.980
You're related to her, right?

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.150
We're in the same series, yes,

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.820
but I'm part of the head family who fell from grace.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:25.160
Sixteen was adopted by Colt when she was young.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:26.700
I see.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:32.340
She became an official American army rifle soon after that.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.210
As you know, she's evolved pretty rapidly

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.340
due to the experience she's gained over the years,

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.970
and she's still being used as an assault rifle today.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.760
It's amazing how many variations she's had.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.480
Oh, but she's not a blood relative of Fourteenonee-san, is she?

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:49.390
That's right.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.900
They're from different families.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:54.570
In terms of a family relation, they'd be sisters-in-law.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.480
So what happened to your branch of the family, anyway?

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.030
I was made after Sixteen, but I didn't sell very well...

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.280
So I became nothing but a memory.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.500
I can't hear you if I'm crying.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.040
So she hasn't shown up yet, huh?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.040
She said she had a shoot today, too.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.040
She's supposed to be on her way here once that's over.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.970
We're starting class now.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.340
AR18, please return to your own class.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.300
Okay.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:26.310
I always thought Sixteen was popular...

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.060
because she was cheap.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.480
You should apologize for putting it like that...

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.100
You two, stop talking!

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.520
Y-Yes, sorry!

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.440
Thanks a lot!

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.070
No, thank you.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.360
See you again, Sixteen-chan.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.530
Oh yeah, who are you featuring next month?

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.240
We were thinking of doing an issue on famous guns around the world.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.990
Probably the AK.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:51.790
Is the M16 really that popular?

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.210
Well, she <i>is</i> lightweight.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.500
Is being lightweight really that important?

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.550
Of course it is.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:01.130
These days it's popular for weapons...

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:06.600
to have modular parts so the operator can use the right combination for the job.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.810
It works by using a rail system where you just attach things to it.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.600
It's really valuable for a gun to be lightweight.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.560
You can carry a lot more bullets that way.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:17.770
What about you, FNC?

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.900
I guess I'm a little on the heavy side.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.110
Only a little, though.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.370
That's not what I meant.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.200
Aren't you going to do a cover shoot, too?

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.000
<i>I embarrassed myself more than I had to...</i>

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.210
Huh?

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.210
So the Japanese teacher said that?

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.670
But I'm not as popular as Sixteen.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.510
So you don't wanna do it, huh?

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.680
I didn't say that...

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:49.680
Then go for it.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.390
But I...

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.690
I was born in Belgium.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.020
I'm 995mm in length.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.320
My weight's a secret.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.360
You're just reading off your specs.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:05.400
That's like meeting someone for the first time and telling them your measurements.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.120
You're mean!

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:11.950
Come on!

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.250
I bet you can think of a better way to show yourself off.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.080
There's a better way?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.790
There is!

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:20.960
Thanks to you, the 5.56mm round became the standard, Funko-chan.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.460
Wow! You sure know a lot!

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.550
I'm talking about you!

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.300
How about showing her how it's done?

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:30.430
Guess I'll have to.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:35.690
The snowy temptress dances in front of you.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:39.940
I pierce your heart from 500 meters

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.530
away.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.870
That was so hot.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.080
I'm not sure that's quite right...

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.370
Yeah yeah.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.000
Sig-chan's already really popular.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.920
I'm not sure I can beat her after that display.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.340
She's used in movies, too.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.960
That's the wrong model!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.630
I won't let a different version steal my thunder!

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:10.510
I don't have any other versions.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.230
Anyway, give it a shot.

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:17.310
R-Right.

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:20.020
You should know me by now.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.900
I'm pretty rare.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:26.320
I'm the FNC!

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.240
This is the state-run Belgian construction facility.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.040
Way to go, Funko-chan.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.410
You're supporting your country.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:40.420
Although, some stuff happened, so we're not state-run anymore.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.170
Funko-chan, keep it up!

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.960
Work it more!

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.170
All right!

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:47.800
From the land of chocolate, comes this diamond in the rough.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.300
You might be surprised,

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.300
but I'm actually pretty good.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.100
Scary.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.100
Wow.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:59.310
You can get a 3.5-cm grouping from 100 meters away!

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.730
You just know you've got the very best here.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:09.530
I'm sorry! I got too full of myself!

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:14.410
I wonder if everyone learned a little bit more about me.

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:19.290
Yeah, but the person who most needs to get people to know her is...

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:34.350
England was the first to predict that the new era of guns

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.850
would prioritize lower calibers and shorter rounds!

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:38.430
They created a bullpup gun,

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.600
using plastic for the hand guard, grip, and other components.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.650
It was supposed to be compact and inexpensive.

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:44.770
In 1985, it was used officially by the army,

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:45.060
What is she doing?
In 1985, it was used officially by the army,

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:46.320
but there were issues.
What is she doing?

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.820
It looks like she wants to say something.
The stubborn and prideful English...

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:49.940
Oh, I've got an idea!

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.410
The girl from the British Empire you'd just love to look after!

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:54.950
You'll be at her side all day.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.790
They say that the more trouble a girl is, the cuter she is.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:00.200
I guess they're adorable once you get used to them.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:02.460
No fair!

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:06.920
Hitting the target or not isn't really a problem in Elle-chan's case.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.550
There's really no other reason to buy her.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.800
Sig, I think you went a little too far.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:17.810
Elle-chan!

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:19.350
Did she break again?

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:23.390
Hey, Sixteen.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:24.310
Hey there.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:25.190
Hey.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:27.650
Must be nice, waltzing in late.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.570
I had work.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:30.570
See you.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:31.570
Talk to you later.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:46.080
I wonder if Elle-chan feels better now.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:47.380
What was that?!

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.630
Why haven't you taken any notes?!

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:50.760
Sixteen-chan?

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.920
You're the one who told me you would!

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:54.430
What were you thinking?

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.390
Oh, Elle-chan wasn't feeling well—

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.060
Fukko, you be quiet!

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:03.730
The questions on the history tests come straight outta the lectures.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.270
What am I gonna do about the next test?

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:08.650
Here you go.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:09.860
Sig...

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:15.570
I can't read German!

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:17.320
Then why don't you use mine?

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.240
I can't read Dutch either!

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:22.040
Did something bad happen?

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:23.620
Not really.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:27.330
I'm just mad that Elle didn't hold up her end of the bargain.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:30.670
Elle told me she'd take notes for me for 100 yen a class.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:34.260
Elle-chan's firing pin broke.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:35.760
She was in the nurse's office...

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.970
You're always breaking.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:41.060
You're a dud.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:42.810
Sixteen-chan!

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:47.900
You know, the word "dud" comes from "person in ragged clothing"?

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:50.770
In World War I, it evolved into "shell that didn't explode".

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:52.320
Now it's used for "expensive failure".

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:04.950
Elle-chan!

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:06.830
Elle-chan?

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:09.330
What happened?

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.170
It was just...

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:34.610
Elle?

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:39.240
Why are you out here?

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:42.240
How unusual.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.870
Are Funko and the others not with you?

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:49.670
See you later.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.510
Sixteen-senpai!

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.220
It's almost time for the tournament.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.850
I'll be rooting for you.

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:03.600
Thanks.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.430
Can I have your autograph?

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:06.140
Sure.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:08.640
Thank you so much.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:22.200
M16...

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:27.450
We'll be the ones who bathe you in blood.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.710
One, two, one, two, one, two...

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.090
One, two, one, two, one, two, one...

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.510
Man, it's hot.
One, two, one, two, one, two, one...

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:40.970
One, two, one, two, one, two, one...

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:44.180
It's almost time for Sixteen and the other girls to have their team battle.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.600
It's their chance to show their capabilities as guns.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.680
A lot of girls managed to hit the big time this way.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.480
Where are they holding it this time?

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:56.190
It's only a rumor, but I heard it's going to be a jungle battle.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:57.150
Really?

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.150
That'll be pretty hard for them.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:00.440
Yeah.

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:04.160
Honestly, I'm pretty tired of the jungle already.

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:08.870
I'm sure Sixteen can't wait.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.620
She might end up facing the transfer students.

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.420
Transfer students?

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.330
Derivatives of the AK.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:20.460
The Finnish Sako Rk. 95, and the Israeli Galil AR.

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:21.010
Seriously?!

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:24.720
They're from the West and they still copied the AK?! Traitors!

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:26.100
Damn it!

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:29.470
If we were in that fight, we'd totally tear them apart.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:30.640
Stupid AKs!

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.480
They're not actually AKs...

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:33.770
<b>Curly's Shop</b>

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:35.100
Welcome.
<b>Curly's Shop</b>

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.530
Where are the dot sights?

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:46.240
The dot sight is an optical device that allows you to aim quicker.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:49.830
It projects a dot of light on a screen, identifying your target.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:52.830
In order to widen the field of sight, the lens is 1x.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:55.040
It's not very useful for precise shots.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:56.750
Hey, Sixteen-chan.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.040
Hey man, where are your dot sights?

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.460
Up top on the shelf to the right.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.510
Right.

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:06.260
And don't call me "man". The name's Curly.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:07.260
Cu—

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:08.720
Don't, Fukko.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:10.640
If you ask, everybody loses.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:12.930
How much is this dot sight, man?

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.310
What's wrong, Sixteen?

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.890
You're not being very friendly.

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:19.310
You plan on attaching a dot sight and doing some CQB?

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.820
I've got a team match coming up.

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:24.780
Oh, who's your partner this year?

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:29.200
You were paired with Sig last year and won pretty easily, right?

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:32.370
I won't be with Sig this time, but I won't lose.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.910
Carrying it all on your shoulders, huh?

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:41.590
Now that we've transferred to this school,

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:46.510
you won't be winning, Sixteen-han.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:48.680
Who are you guys?

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:50.600
I'm Sako,

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:52.350
and this is Galil.

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:01.110
Sig-chan!

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:06.950
Isn't there a severe punishment
for using a gun outside of the school grounds, Sig-han?

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:10.450
You two will be the ones who determine whether I use it or not.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.210
<i>It doesn't look like there are any bullets in the see-through magazine.</i>

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.250
<i>Is she bluffing?</i>

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:18.580
<i>No...</i>

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:22.960
<i>If she reloaded, she could still have two shots: one bullet in the chamber and another at the top.</i>

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:26.380
<i>With Sig's skills, that's all she'd need.</i>

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:28.720
<i>Maybe it's a trap?</i>

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.990
You got us this time, Sig-han.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:50.070
I'm looking forward to our team battle.

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:50.950
See you.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:54.120
Huh? What was that?

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:58.000
The Sako Rk. 95 and the Galil AR.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:03.380
They use the same standard 5.56mm NATO rounds as you,

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:06.510
but their origins can be traced back to the Kalashnikov and the old Soviet Union.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:13.800
Sixteen, you have history with them.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:20.690
In the 1960s, in a wet, humid jungle, where it was dark even in the afternoon,

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:24.230
the assault rifles of America and the Soviet Union squared off.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.360
The American army used the M14 as its weapon of choice,

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:32.660
but its wooden stock and long length weren't suited for the jungle.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.660
They quickly developed a version with a smaller,

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:37.080
lightweight form factor and put that to use instead.

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:41.920
The M16, a new lower caliber, high-velocity assault rifle, was born.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:46.170
Meanwhile, the Soviets' Avtomat Kalashnikova

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:49.340
had a compact body measuring only 874mm

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:52.050
and was capable of operating in mud and sand,

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.890
making it a masterpiece that the soldiers had faith in.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:59.470
During the M16's initial stages of use, the gun had problems

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:02.810
when it wasn't properly cleaned or when the wrong gunpowder was used.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:07.020
But because it was so light in combat, soldiers began to have faith in it.

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:10.900
But the M16 was unable to bring victory for America,

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:17.530
who began withdrawing in 1969, thereby ending the Vietnam War.

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:20.200
I haven't lost.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:24.210
I won't be able to watch your back next time.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.000
I know that.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.000
Your partner is important.

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:32.420
Sixteen-chan...

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:39.510
Hey, Sixteen-chan.

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:40.270
Elle-chan...

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.520
I'm done.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.310
Sixteen-chan,

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.520
aren't you worried about Elle-chan?

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:50.650
Sixteen-chan!

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:56.200
Oh, there you are.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.240
Fal-senpai is on the phone for you.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.660
Did something happen?

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.210
I don't mind Elle following me around,

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:04.540
but she hasn't said a word.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.170
What's she doing now?

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:09.420
She's taking a bath with Fourteen.

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:12.630
You can do whatever you want with me.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:13.970
Just kidding.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:16.720
Didn't you hear me?

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:16.890
I'll let her stay here tonight.
Didn't you hear me?

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:18.760
You can do whatever you want with me.
I'll let her stay here tonight.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:19.180
You can do whatever you want with me.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:21.720
What should I do?

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:25.060
<i>Just do what you think is best.</i>

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.940
What I think is best...

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.440
Hey, Fal!

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:30.690
Get me a towel!

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:32.110
Wait a minute!

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:34.740
Good luck, Funko.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:36.910
Thanks.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:41.580
You done?

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:47.790
I love Sixteen-chan and Elle-chan equally!

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.630
I don't want the two of them fighting.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.250
I want them to make up somehow.

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:57.550
Those two are such pains in the neck, aren't they?

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:01.850
Did you see?

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.150
A tropical rainforest...

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:09.690
I see.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:13.190
So that's why they're acting all high and mighty.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:18.070
I won't lose this time, you fake AKs.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:22.330
Elle-chan isn't coming.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:23.990
It doesn't matter.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:25.000
But...

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:26.870
Teams, to the battlefield!

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:31.040
Let's go!

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:43.350
Get on, Elle!

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:44.890
Do you plan on leaving Sixteen alone out there?!

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:52.940
Gather around!

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:55.690
Listen up, kids!

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.150
Sir, yes, sir!

00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:00.700
Our stage this time will be this jungle area,

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:04.030
200 meters by 300 meters.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:05.290
Sir, yes, sir!

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:08.000
There's a water feature in the center,

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.040
but as you can see, it's mostly rainforest.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.920
Combat will be restricted to close-range.

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:16.670
Therefore, this tournament will be full contact.

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:19.220
Bring subsonic ammo and body armor.

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.390
You girls are guns!

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:22.720
If you get hit, you won't die,

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.890
but be prepared for some pain!

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.060
Dismissed!

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:36.230
Eighteen-chan, how many rounds are you taking?

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:40.570
Two with 38 rounds and one with 24 rounds.

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:43.490
I'll take four with 25 rounds each.

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:44.950
What about you, Sixteen-chan?

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.240
It's a secret.

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:48.410
I might be up against your team later.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:51.330
Are you going to fight by yourself?

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:53.960
Of course!

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:56.920
<i>The first round will be starting shortly.</i>

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:58.920
<i>Participants will wait at their respective coordinates.</i>

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:03.510
I was thinking of heading back to my home town once practice is over.

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:05.640
So I want to win.

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:07.640
Don't jinx us.

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:10.390
Hey, will Sixteen-chan...

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:13.400
Funko-chan, just focus on the match for now.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:15.560
Right.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:18.480
That's the signal.

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.240
You take point, Eighteen-chan.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.400
I'm fine with that, but let's...

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:24.780
really knock 'em dead this time.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:26.280
Sounds good.

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:40.010
<i>Their point man is already over here.</i>

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:43.260
<i>They're close.</i>

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:47.010
<i>Their rear gunner should still be back at their defense line.</i>

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:48.220
<i>I can do this.</i>

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.470
<i>I need to trap their point first!</i>

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.780
<i>I can't lose!</i>

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.750
<i>Team Echo only has Sixteen.</i>

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:21.250
<i>If she's over there,</i>

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:22.920
<i>then there's no one guarding her flag.</i>

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:24.840
<i>Sorry for you, but...</i>

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:26.800
<i>You're dead meat.</i>

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:34.180
Good for you, Sixteen-chan.

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:35.940
What'd you expect?

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:39.230
I can't bite the dust yet.

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.770
Sixteen-chan...

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:44.030
Fukko, you don't have time to worry about others right now.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:02.590
Let's tear another page off our calendar

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:10.100
Together we braved

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:22.070
past ages and never-ending conflict

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:29.660
Together we laughed and cried in those hectic times

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:35.290
When I ran

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:48.720
I put my footsteps into the ground

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:56.430
Let's tear another page off our calendar

00:22:57.390 --> 00:23:03.610
Something is bound to change

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:11.740
One by one the days I tore off pile up

00:23:12.280 --> 00:23:15.660
like a past I cannot erase

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:21.830
They will be my strength for days to come

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:28.720
We're going nowhere fast!

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:33.430
It must be tough, Sixteen-han.

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:34.930
We've got nothing to worry about.

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:36.390
Let's go do something bad.

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:37.180
Next time:

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:37.680
Graze it!

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:38.810
Beat it!

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:39.770
It's fine.
